# Feuerbach's theorem (tangency distance form) — the nine-point circle is internally tangent to the incircle: NI = R/2 − r (source: Feuerbach 1822)
A B C = triangle
O = circumcenter(A, B, C)
N = nine_point_center(A, B, C)
I = incenter(A, B, C)
T = foot(I, line(B, C))
prove 2 * dist(N, I) = dist(O, A) - 2 * dist(I, T)
